{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T05:13:38.060Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1706"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1706: a stale session-state lock makes pm release clear the claim and then exit 4, --force repeats the refusal, and claim only warns"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1706 (filed 2026-11-11). A stale session-state lock (expired TTL from a crashed agent) makes claim and release disagree, and release reports failure after it has written. On a fresh tracker: pm claim exits 0 with the claim_semantic_attribution_unrecorded warning and records the claim; pm release exits 4 with 'Item session-state lock is stale; rerun with --force when supported for this command' but the claim is already removed; pm release --force exits 4 with the same text; pm health reports stale_lock_count 1 with remedy pm gc --scope locks. Four problems: a partial write reported as a failure, two policies for one condition, a recovery hint naming a flag that cannot succeed, and wording that attributes the lock to an item. Expected: release refuses before any mutation or succeeds with the same attribution warning claim uses; one policy for a stale session-state lock across claim, start, release and close (reclaiming an expired TTL automatically is simplest); the refusal or warning names pm gc --scope locks and the lock path and never recommends an unusable flag. pm-rust mirrors the published behaviour (pm-rust#165)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","concurrency","gh:1706","locking","recovery"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:38.060Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:38.060Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"release never mutates and then exits non-zero on a stale session-state lock; claim, start, release and close share one policy for a stale session-state lock; The refusal or warning names pm gc --scope locks and the lock path, never an unusable flag, and attributes the lock to session state"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-dj98"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"One consistent outcome for a stale session-state lock with a working recovery"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"release removes the claim then exits 4; --force repeats the refusal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-d70h","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:38.060Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"861dfb2973f6dec88bed76b40be495a15c265668fd3a84580937770416df6d99","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":