{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T15:22:40.744Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1f65549d969a385dd658b1e6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1706","claim:pm-gh1716","claim:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1706+pm-gh1716+pm-jndg9a","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1706","claim:pm-gh1716","claim:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-jndg9a","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T15:22:40.744Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-13T15:22:40.744Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Progress (branch fix/mutation-outcome-honesty): reproduced on the 2026.11.13 build (claim exit 0 with the attribution warning, release exit 4 after clearing the claim, release --force exit 4). Root cause: mutateSessionState acquired its singleton lock with force_required_for_stale_lock hard-coded true and force false, so an expired lease could never be reclaimed by any command, and runRelease awaited the attribution write after the item commit without the warning wrapper claim uses. Fix: the session-state lease is reclaimed past its TTL (the same policy the context usage ledger and workspace transaction locks already use); claim and release share recordAttributionAfterCommit, which returns claim_semantic_attribution_unrecorded or release_semantic_attribution_unrecorded plus a suggestion naming the refusal code and pm gc --scope locks; the stale-lock refusal is now typed stale_lock_requires_override with details lock_id and tracker-relative lock_path and no longer says Item for non-item locks. Close does not write session state, so it has no stale-lock path. Negative control: restoring the old lock policy fails the new stale-session-lock spec."}]}],"before_hash":"3045487be02fcca467bd04f046dcc2bcc4303c1a177caf66defbfa6af6104999","after_hash":"3018ab7590eb02914186996d4459b92054bd508e3498266c2837ec8315d3bc08","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"da41a66e05a0258cf2450e16336e41d06bbd36fddbef18c783ccaf25af535c10"}
