{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-13T18:02:28.967Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1f65549d969a385dd658b1e6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.323","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-13T18:02:28.967Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2 (Codex, CodeRabbit): (1) pm gc keeps a lock whose metadata cannot be read or dated, so the stale-lock refusal now names an owner-verified manual removal for those instead of a gc that changes nothing. (2) refusalCode checks the context shape again, so an error named PmCliError without a context never escapes the post-commit catch or makes isAlreadyClaimedError throw. (3) the attribution suggestion renders pm health and pm gc --scope locks with the caller's tracker selection. claim and release moved their advice assembly into helpers so both stay under the CodeFactor complexity ceiling of 16."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-13T18:02:28.967Z"}],"before_hash":"b36f75c0acc869678a2269d1c475a29ecf64b0ffa1eefd04d4d3e4960f3852f3","after_hash":"ee18eca6bdc563ffebe5e2f0adb520843dab5e93fb47d696554f2807fcabffb4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"483483f2b08ef313bb8b5c0e4effa7f522f850c3087d08f63377110072e317da"}
